course: dictionary
lesson: 2486
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word dead does not always mean the same thing. Its meaning depends on the words around it, which is its context. «The old tree was dead, so its leaves had all fallen.» Here dead means no longer alive. Nobody thinks the tree is sleeping.
explain: «My phone is dead, so I can't call you.» A phone cannot be alive, so dead here means not working. «The town is dead on Sundays» means very quiet, with nothing happening. Check by swapping in your meaning: does the sentence still make sense?
explain: Dead can also be a small, informal word meaning very or completely. «That test was dead easy» means it was very easy, not that the test had died. «I'm dead» in a chat often means something is so funny that you cannot stop laughing.
explain: Dead also appears in phrases with their own meaning. A dead end is a road that does not go anywhere. When a pet or a person dies, people feel grief, and it is okay to talk about it and to cry.
fact: Dead can be an adjective, as in «dead leaves», or a noun, as in «the dead», meaning dead people.
fact: Dead means no longer alive. Living things grow, breathe, feed and reproduce; dead things do not.
fact: Dead can also mean not working, as in «a dead battery», or very quiet, as in «dead silence».
fact: Informal dead means very or completely, as in «dead tired» or «dead ahead».
fact: Never touch a dead animal, because it can carry germs. A dead battery should go into recycling, not the bin.
exercise: «The old tree was dead, so its leaves had all fallen.» What does dead mean here? | Covered in snow | Fast asleep | Very, very tall | *No longer alive
exercise: «My phone is dead, so I can't call you.» What does dead mean here? | Sad about grief | Very or completely | *Not working | Dead ahead
exercise: «The town is dead on Sundays.» What does dead suggest? | Covered in dust | Lost forever | Full of noise and people | *Very quiet, with nothing happening
test: «I'm dead tired after the match.» What does dead mean in this sentence? | Very quiet | *Very, completely | Not alive | Not working
test: Which sentence uses dead to mean very or completely? | «The dog is dead» | «The road is a dead end» | «The dead leaves fell» | *«That quiz was dead easy»
exam: Ella says «The road is a dead end» means the road is broken. What does dead end mean? | A road with a very sharp bend | A road made of dead leaves | A road that is too short to drive | *A road that does not go anywhere
